            <ArticleTitle>T regulatory cells and allergy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1049-55</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Anergy, tolerance and active suppression may not be independent events, but rather involve similar mechanisms and cell types in immune regulation. Induction of allergen-specific T(Reg) cells seems essential for maintaining a healthy immune response towards allergens. By utilizing multiple secreted cytokines and surface molecules, antigen-specific T(Reg) cells may re-direct an inappropriate immune response against allergens or auto-antigens.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
